    "confidence": "high",
    "needs_review": [
      "LaunchDarkly takes the API access token raw in the Authorization header (no Bearer prefix), which the scaffolded auth already encodes",
      "list_environments deliberately picks only key/name/color/tags/critical/defaultTtl: the raw environment payload also carries apiKey and mobileKey, which are live SDK credentials and must never be returned to an agent",
      "list_flags passes summary=true so the response stays the per-environment summary rather than full targeting rules, which blow past the 2000-char truncate on any real project",
      "probe hints use the project key 'default', LaunchDarkly's own documented starter project, so the route is exercised with a realistic key shape rather than a random string"
    ]
